    "evidence": "Set A=U=V=I_2, H=[[1,1/2],[1/2,1]], and R=(1/sqrt(2))*[[1,1],[1,-1]]. Then R^2=I and RA=AR, while RHR^T=diag(3/2,1/2). The group average (H+RHR^T)/2 has diagonal (5/4,3/4), not (1,1). This refutes an arbitrary-orthogonal-action extension, but does not refute the explicitly permutation-scoped source proof.",
